# Phase 5 — Storage & Recovery

## Overview

Phase 5 focused on making the PostgreSQL data warehouse resilient to pod failures and establishing a reliable database backup and recovery mechanism.

The objective was not only to deploy PostgreSQL on the K3s cluster, but also to prove that the warehouse data remains available after infrastructure-level failures and can be restored independently from a PostgreSQL backup.

The recovery architecture implemented in this phase consists of:

```text
                    ┌──────────────────────┐
                    │    PostgreSQL 18     │
                    │   DataWarehouse DB    │
                    └──────────┬───────────┘
                               │
                               ▼
                    ┌──────────────────────┐
                    │   PersistentVolume   │
                    │        20 GiB         │
                    └──────────┬───────────┘
                               │
                               ▼
                    ┌──────────────────────┐
                    │  PersistentVolumeClaim│
                    │     postgres-pvc     │
                    └──────────┬───────────┘
                               │
                               ▼
                    ┌──────────────────────┐
                    │    K3s local-path    │
                    │       Storage        │
                    └──────────────────────┘
```

---

## Phase 5 Objectives

The main objectives were:

* Configure and verify persistent PostgreSQL storage.
* Verify the PersistentVolumeClaim and PersistentVolume.
* Establish a database recovery baseline.
* Simulate PostgreSQL pod failure.
* Verify automatic Kubernetes pod recovery.
* Verify that persistent data survives pod failure.
* Create a PostgreSQL database backup.
* Verify backup integrity.
* Perform a complete database restore into a separate recovery database.
* Validate the restored warehouse.
* Document the recovery process.

