# 5.3 Kubernetes Pod Failure Simulation

To test persistent storage recovery, the PostgreSQL pod was intentionally deleted.

The original pod was:

```text
postgres-747d4b6d84-q7r44
```

It was deleted using:

```bash
sudo kubectl delete pod -n datawarehouse postgres-747d4b6d84-q7r44
```

The pod deletion was intentional and used as a controlled failure test.

Because PostgreSQL was managed by a Kubernetes Deployment, Kubernetes automatically created a replacement pod.

The replacement pod became:

```text
postgres-747d4b6d84-7jbwq
```

and reached:

```text
1/1 Running
```

This demonstrated Kubernetes self-healing behavior.

### Recovery flow

```text
PostgreSQL Pod
      │
      │ Intentional failure
      ▼
Pod deleted
      │
      ▼
Kubernetes Deployment detects missing replica
      │
      ▼
New PostgreSQL Pod created
      │
      ▼
Persistent storage attached
      │
      ▼
PostgreSQL becomes Ready
```

