# 5.4 Data Persistence Verification

After the replacement PostgreSQL pod became ready, the warehouse was queried again.

The result was:

```text
fact_stock_prices = 619,017
```

The data quality table was also checked:

```text
data_quality_errors = 12
```

The values were identical to the pre-failure baseline.

### Recovery validation

```text
BEFORE FAILURE             AFTER RECOVERY
─────────────────          ─────────────────
619,017 fact rows    →     619,017 fact rows
12 quality errors    →     12 quality errors
```

This proved that deleting the PostgreSQL pod did not delete the database contents.

The persistence mechanism successfully allowed the replacement pod to access the existing database storage.

